   `diskGlueQuotHomeoSphere n h : DiskGlueQuot n h ≃ₜ Sphere (n+1)` for an **arbitrary** `h : 𝕊ⁿ ≃ₜ 𝕊ⁿ` — two `(n+1)`-disks glued along their boundary form `𝕊ⁿ⁺¹` regardless of the gluing homeomorphism. Includes the relation transport, compatibility with the earlier `doubleDiskQuotHomeoSphere` (`diskGlueQuotHomeoSphere_refl_apply`), and compact/T2/nonempty instances of the quotient.

2. **`SphereOfTwoDisks.lean`** (1 decl) — **closed-cover recognition on an actual topological space**: `sphereOfTwoDisks` proves that a compact Hausdorff `X = A ∪ B` with closed `A, B ≅ 𝔻ⁿ⁺¹` meeting in the boundary sphere of the first chart is `≃ₜ 𝕊ⁿ⁺¹`. The comparison map `q : X → DiskGlueQuot n h` has an explicit two-sided inverse by quotient recursion, so it is a continuous bijection; compactness + the T2 instance close it. (The symmetric second-chart hypothesis proved unnecessary and was dropped — the statement is strictly stronger.)

3. **`TwoHemisphereInstance.lean`** (19 decls) — the **non-vacuity instance**: the mirrored chart `upperHemisphereHomeoDisk n : UpperHemisphere n ≃ₜ Disk n`, the named hypothesis inputs (`lowerHemisphere_isClosed`, `upperHemisphere_isClosed`, `hemisphere_cover`, `lowerHemisphere_boundary_eq_inter`, `hemisphere_charts_agree`), and `sphereOfTwoDisks_hemisphere_instance`, which applies the closed-cover theorem to the two-hemisphere decomposition of `𝕊ⁿ⁺¹`.

